From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:39:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 134/148] docs(ci): drop the stale "module" wording from
 pack-release-compatibility's gascity_ref (gcp-fooz4)

gc is installed from the release archive, and `main` now means the
rolling edge pre-release rather than a Go module query. The listed
values were already right.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml b/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
index b3e3dcd7..ab6ea621 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ on:
   workflow_dispatch:
     inputs:
       gascity_ref:
-        description: "Gas City module ref/version to install, such as latest, main, or v0.3.0."
+        description: "Gas City ref/version to install, such as latest, main, or v0.3.0."
         required: false
         default: latest
       registry_ref:
